LSCAN1
# LakeShark conventional scan list - everything, Franklin NH to Provincetown MA
#
#     python tools/sd_put.py tools/scanlist_all.lscan scanlist_all.lscan PORT
#     ch load /sdcard/scanlist_all.lscan
#
# This is the whole list. There is nothing to switch between and nothing to
# reload on the road: 63 channels in eight zones, laid out north to south, and
# LOCATION filtering decides what is worth scanning from the GPS fix. Drive
# from Franklin to Provincetown and the list follows you down without being
# touched.
#
# scanlist_nh_ma.lscan and scanlist_cape_cod.lscan are the two halves of this
# file and are kept for a shorter list. Loading either one REPLACES everything,
# which is how Franklin PD goes missing after loading the Cape half.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ZONES
#
#     0  wide area      NH statewide, BAPERN, interop, amateur calling
#     1  Franklin       Franklin PD, Lakes Region fire, Troop E
#     2  Concord        Merrimack County, Concord PD, capital area fire
#     3  south NH       Troop B, Plymouth County
#     4  mid Cape       canal, Barnstable County, Yarmouth, Dennis
#     5  lower Cape     Brewster, Harwich, Chatham, Orleans
#     6  outer Cape     Eastham, Wellfleet, Truro, Provincetown, Seashore
#     7  marine and EMS marine, Coast Guard, CMED, NOAA
#
# Eight is the firmware limit, so geography does the rest through LOCATION.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT IS HERE AND WHAT IS NOT
#
# P25 is 16 of the 63: NH State Police, Franklin PD, Merrimack and Concord,
# BAPERN, Plymouth County and the Cape Cod National Seashore.
#
# Town POLICE from Brewster east to Provincetown are talkgroups on the county
# 800 MHz trunk and cannot be followed conventionally, so those towns carry no
# police entry. Yarmouth PD is conventional 800 and is here, as are the four
# shared Barnstable County VHF police channels.
#
# Town FIRE is the opposite: every Cape town simulcasts its fire alarm
# dispatch on its own 33 MHz LOW BAND channel in clear analogue. That is the
# one thing a conventional receiver follows the whole way out.
#
# LOW BAND CAVEAT: 33 MHz sits 9 MHz above the bottom of the R820T2 range, so
# those are the weakest channels here and reward a longer antenna.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FIELD ORDER
#     name|freq_hz|MODE|zone|latitude|longitude|radius_km|priority
#
# MODE is P25 or NFM only. Every field must be present; '#' starts a comment.
#
# SOURCING: 154.7850 Franklin PD is the only frequency here the board has
# actually decoded. The rest come from published listener references, so treat
# a silent channel as unconfirmed rather than broken. One known conflict:
# Harwich fire alarm is listed as 33.94 by one source and 33.96 by another,
# and 33.94 is used here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

